<title>SWEDEN: Few Swedish players see Sweden in EMU from start.</title>
<headline>Few Swedish players see Sweden in EMU from start.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Only 15 percent of players in Sweden's debt and share markets believe Sweden will join Economic and Monetary Union (EMU) from the outset, according to a poll by TEMO and Ohman Fondkommission brokerage.</p>
<p>TEMO, a market research institute, corrected its original figures.  </p>
<p>In the poll, the first in a regular series from TEMO and Ohmans, 42 percent of market players said they believed the Swedish crown would be linked to the EU's Exchange Rate Mechanism (ERM) before the parliament takes a decision on membership next year.</p>
<p>Some 72 market players were interviewed for the poll, which was carried out on Tuesday and Wednesday this week.</p>
<p>TEMO said its Finance Markets Index would be published monthly.</p>
<p>-- Simon Haydon, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1004</p>
